": "ABSTAIN_NOT_ADMITTED", "answer_or_proposed": " 10 (fugitives);  10 (fugitives);  10 (fugitives); 5 million (offer)", "marker": "NOT_ADMISSIBLE", "harvest": "NEEDS_JUDGE"}, "traits": {"outcome": "ABSTAIN_NOT_ADMITTED", "answer_or_proposed": "not run", "marker": "NOT_ADMISSIBLE", "harvest": "NEEDS_JUDGE", "reason": "pending slow clock", "provisional": true}, "topic_node": {"outcome": "ANSWER_PROVISIONAL", "answer_or_proposed": "medtop:02000000", "marker": "BELOW_BAR", "harvest": "DISCARD"}}, "total_ms": 459.17, "over_budget": false, "seq": 5, "read_at": 1795539828.2074156, "lag_s": 268299.15, "gaps": ["UNPLACED_HIGH", "NOT_ATTACHED"]}, "text": "Mexico's military captures drug kingpin on FBI's most wanted list. Mexico's military says it has captured the leader of a drug trafficking group among the 10 most wanted fugitives sought by US law enforcement. Fausto Isidro Meza — whose alias is \"Chapo Isidro\" — and two other leaders of his gang were captured during a special forces raid in Sinaloa state. The kingpin faces criminal charges in both Mexico and the United States. Mexico's military says it has captured the leader of a drug trafficking group among the 10 most wanted fugitives sought by US law enforcement. Fausto Isidro Meza — whose alias is \"Chapo Isidro\" — and two other leaders of his gang were captured during a special forces raid on Friday night, local time, in Sinaloa state, the Mexican National Defense Secretariat announced on X. Giving his name as Fausto Isidro Meza-Flores, the FBI listed him as one of their 10 most wanted fugitives and the alleged leader of the Beltran Leyva gang, which is allied with one of two rival factions in the powerful Sinaloa cartel. The FBI had offered a $US5 million ($7.55 million) reward for information leading to his arrest. The US intelligence organisation's bulletin says his group is responsible for importing \"large quantities of heroin, methamphetamine, cocaine, fentanyl, and marijuana into the United States\". He was captured alongside his number two in the group and another man identified as a financial operator. The Mexican government said in an early Saturday report that intelligence from the Trump administration helped authorities capture him, but provided few details about how the two countries coordinated. Videos and photos from the city of Guasave, Sinaloa — where Meza Flores was captured — show screaming civilians fleeing gunfire at a baseball game, as well as burnt cars. Mexican authorities said they used \"stealth and surprise\" to capture him. They said after being attacked with guns and explosives from likely cartel operatives, the officials entered a home and arrested him. They later evacuated Meza Flores and others detained in the clash in a Mexican Air Force plane to Mexico City. He faces criminal charges in both Mexico and the United States.", "stages_full": {"windows": {"windows": 10, "cap": 12, "pct_body_read": 100, "offsets_text": [[67, 260], [261, 483], [484, 681], [682, 879], [880, 1079], [1079, 1291], [1291, 1568], [1569, 1790], [1791, 2042], [2042, 2193]]}, "scan_dates": {"spots": {"attribution": 6, "date": 2, "entity": 33, "event": 7, "modal": 1, "money": 1, "quote": 4}, "dates": [["Friday", "2026-11-20"], ["Saturday", "2026-11-21"]], "dates_resolved": 2, "anchor": "2026-11-21", "time_proxy": {"label": "time_proxy", "marker": "PROVISIONAL", "offset_days": [-1, 0], "n": 2, "of": "resolved date minus published date, in days"}}, "facts": {"kinds": {"amount": 10, "date": 2, "name": 33, "triple": 28}, "stated": 37, "unbound": 36, "invalid": 0, "stated_amount": 10, "stated_date": 1, "quarantined": 0, "held": [], "items": [{"kind": "amount", "s": 154, "e": 157, "text": " 10", "status": "stated"}, {"kind": "amount", "s": 518, "e": 521, "text": " 10", "status": "stated"}, {"kind": "amount", "s": 888, "e": 891, "text": " 10", "status": "stated"}, {"kind": "amount", "s": 1068, "e": 1077, "text": "5 million", "status": "stated"}, {"kind": "amount", "s": 1079, "e": 10